{"name":"Raisin in the Sun","hex":"#78615c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"raisin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dried grape."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Of fruit: to dry out; to become like raisins.","To flavor (an alcoholic beverage) with fruit that has raisined."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raisin"},{"term":"sun","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Sundanese."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The star that is closest to the Earth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sun"}],"entries":[{"title":"A Raisin in the Sun","blocks":[{"text":"A Raisin in the Sun is a play by Lorraine Hansberry that debuted on Broadway in 1959. The title comes from the poem \"Harlem\" by Langston Hughes. The story tells of a black family's experiences on the south side of Chicago, as they attempt to improve their financial circumstances with an insurance payout following the death of their patriarch, and deals with matters of housing discrimination, racism, and assimilation. The New York Drama Critics' Circle named it the best play of 1959, and in the 21st century publications such as The Independent and Time Out have listed it among the best plays ever written."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/%22A_Raisin_in_the_Sun%22%2C_by_Lorraine_Hansberry.jpg/330px-%22A_Raisin_in_the_Sun%22%2C_by_Lorraine_Hansberry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Raisin_in_the_Sun"},{"title":"Raisin","blocks":[{"text":"A raisin is a dried grape. Raisins are produced in many regions of the world and may be eaten raw or used in cooking, baking, and brewing. The word raisin is commonly used for the dried dark-colored seedless grape, while sultana is a golden-colored dried grape, and currant is a dried small Black Corinth seedless grape."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Raisins_01.jpg/330px-Raisins_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raisin"},{"title":"Sun","blocks":[{"text":"The Sun is the star located at the centre of the Solar System. It is a massive sphere of hot plasma, heated to incandescence by nuclear fusion reactions in its core, radiating the energy from its surface mainly as visible light and infrared radiation, with 10% at ultraviolet energies. It is the main source of energy for life on Earth. The Sun has been an object of veneration in many cultures and a central subject of astronomical research since antiquity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/330px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/A_Raisin_in_the_Sun_1959.JPG/500px-A_Raisin_in_the_Sun_1959.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/A_Raisin_in_the_Sun_1959.JPG/500px-A_Raisin_in_the_Sun_1959.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Scene from the play. Ruby Dee as Ruth, Claudia McNeil as Lena, Glynn Turman as Travis, Sidney Poitier as Walter, and John Fiedler as Karl Lindner.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_Raisin_in_the_Sun_1959.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Raisins_2.jpg/500px-Raisins_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Raisins_2.jpg/500px-Raisins_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Golden raisins (sultanas)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARaisins_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Grape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg/500px-Grape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Grape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg/1280px-Grape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Grape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg/500px-Grape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"California seedless grape raisins (left) and California Zante currants","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Nearly_Dried_Raisins.jpg/330px-Nearly_Dried_Raisins.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Nearly_Dried_Raisins.jpg/330px-Nearly_Dried_Raisins.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sun-drying raisins","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANearly_Dried_Raisins.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Raisin_sale_at_khari_baoli_market%2C_Delhi.jpg/500px-Raisin_sale_at_khari_baoli_market%2C_Delhi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Raisin_sale_at_khari_baoli_market%2C_Delhi.jpg/1280px-Raisin_sale_at_khari_baoli_market%2C_Delhi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Raisin_sale_at_khari_baoli_market%2C_Delhi.jpg/500px-Raisin_sale_at_khari_baoli_market%2C_Delhi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&